<h1>Julia Ramirez</h1>
<p>12th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.ramirezfor12.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (ramirezfor12.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Filed nominating petitions for reelection on Oct. 19, 2026. Her campaign site names Feb. 23, 2027 as Election Day and keeps the issue platform from her 2023 race, which calls for investment in education, public safety, local economic development, housing, community health, and environmental justice.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>12th Ward alderwoman since 2023; social worker and restorative justice practitioner with Chicago Public Schools, with earlier work at Latinos Progresando, Instituto del Progreso Latino, and the Back of the Yards Neighborhood Council.</p>
